    "updated_at": "2022-07-05T16:29:47Z",
    "body": "FWIW, I do have a path forward for addressing this issue within the Workers implementation that does not require any public API changes. The changes are entirely internal to the implementation of the data queuing and backpressure signaling in `ReadableStreamDefaultController` and `ReadableByteStreamController` and `ReadableStream` without having any impact on public API (both consumer and producer sides). The external facing API pieces discussed in my original post above (e.g. the non-exclusive reader class) can be considered to be optional to resolving this.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
